      "content": "It is very risky to self-medicate with old antibiotics, even if you suspect a bacterial infection. If your tonsils look red and swollen, you should absolutely try to get an appointment, but if you can't, consider a telehealth consultation first. For now, focus on managing symptoms with warm salt water gargles and plenty of fluids until a professional can properly assess you.",
      "source": "target",
